# Cyber X website · the settings it reads
#
# 1. Copy this file and name the copy  .env.local
# 2. Fill in the values in .env.local on your own laptop.
#
# Settings live in two places only: .env.local here, and Vercel's
# Environment Variables. Never paste a key into the code, a chat or a
# screenshot. Test keys only: the website refuses to build or start with any
# key that looks live.
#
# This file holds names, never values, so it is safe to share.

# --- W0 · Setup ------------------------------------------------------------

# The two Cyber X addresses (no domain for the demo). On a laptop leave them
# out: they default to http://localhost:3000 (the app) and
# http://localhost:3001 (this website). On Vercel both must be set, in both
# projects, as full https:// addresses with nothing after the name.
# APP_URL=https://cyber-x-eosin.vercel.app
# WEBSITE_URL=

# --- W2 · Sign in and freeze ------------------------------------------------

# The website's own database login (cyberx_website): it can only run the
# website's functions and can read no table. On Vercel: Supabase's
# transaction pooler address, with the user cyberx_website.<project ref> and
# the password set by hand in Supabase's SQL editor. Without it the website
# still opens, and sign-in says "We can't reach Cyber X right now".
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://cyberx_website.<project-ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres
# The line to Supabase is always encrypted. To also check it really is
# Supabase (optional): paste the certificate from Supabase → Database
# settings → SSL configuration → Download certificate. It is public, not a
# secret; line breaks may be written as \n.
# DATABASE_CA_CERT=-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\n...\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----

# Test mode (texts are off): the sign-in code shows on the screen only for
# these numbers, so nobody can sign in as someone else by knowing their
# alias. Written any way the sign-in box accepts, with commas between; a
# number start followed by * covers every number beginning with it.
# SMS_TEST_NUMBERS=0801 234 5678, +2348030000001

# Only for the phone and desktop tests: a throwaway LOCAL Postgres, never
# the real project (scripts/db/test-db.mjs refuses anything else).
# E2E_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
# E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/cyberx_web_e2e
